                <pb facs="0270" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00 Revolutions/57: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McCafferty</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-16T17:00:00-07:00">December 16, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:44 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>104. A revolution apparently started at 4 p.m. today. There is firing in various
                    parts of the city. I have not yet been able to obtain any information, but I
                    believe it is a revolt of the Army against the Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McCafferty</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
